    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate is headlined by **Corbin Carroll**, who commands the highest score of the day at 84.65. His matchup against Mitch Keller is prime for production; while the catcher\u2019s arm introduces a minor penalty for stolen base attempts, **Corbin Carroll**\u2019s aggressive approach from the lead-off spot remains our most reliable engine for R and SB. **James Wood** follows closely with a 78.42, benefiting from an elite xwOBA of 0.420 and a favorable tilt against a struggling Max Scherzer. Similarly, **Jose Caballero** (71.83) earns a \"Strong\" start designation, as his platoon advantage against a weak lefty like Schultz allows him to overcome a lower batting order position, making him a critical weapon for our scarcity-driven focus on speed.\n\nWe have a clear platoon edge working in favor of **Isaac Paredes** (71.15) and **Josh Naylor** (66.83), both of whom capitalize on favorable right-on-right matchups to push their efficiency scores deep into the \"Strong\" tier. **Brice Turang** also sees a boost to 66.57 thanks to favorable wind conditions and a spot in the #3 hole. On the bench, **Henry Bolte** was the most difficult exclusion with a 51.08 score; while he benefits from a strong park factor and a solid platoon look against a lefty, he ultimately falls behind our starters because we require the higher volume of plate appearances and specific category contributions offered by the likes of **Zach McKinstry** and **Tyler Soderstrom**.\n\nRisk management remains a priority heading into tonight\u2019s games. We are monitoring a 31% rain risk for **Austin Riley**, which creates a non-trivial threat of an early exit or cold-plate performance; coupled with his #7 batting position and a stiff test against a talented left-handed arm, he is a fringe start at 54.87. We have also factored in the lack of opportunity for **Vinnie Pasquantino** today due to the schedule, and we are proceeding cautiously with **Cole Young**, as his #1 spot in the order is offset by the need to navigate a tricky matchup against Rocker. We remain heavily indexed toward **James Wood** and **Corbin Carroll** to carry the load if these secondary options face unforeseen volatility.",
